sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) & Pinet et al. (2019) Picasso tadpole craniofacial attractor remodeling — MorphoEval overall 92.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py` (92.1/100, up from 57.8/100 in Pass 1; +34.3 overall). The remediated script integrates the coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE with inter-organ relational spring coupling C_ij via 4th-order Runge-Kutta across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45->65, proving strict monotonic Lyapunov energy decay V(X) -> 0 and reproducing all 6 canonical Vandenberg et al. (2012) and Pinet et al. (2019) regimes: Wild-Type remodeling (`D_P = 0.0005`), Picasso scrambled closed-loop (`D_P = 0.0009`, bilateral asymmetry `0.715 -> 0.0002`, 99.97% symmetry restoration), Caudal lateral eye rotation (`D_P = 0.0007`), Lateral jaw/mouth translocation (`D_P = 0.0007`), Open-loop fixed-vector null hypothesis (`D_P = 0.3439`, preserving exact initial defect), and GM6001 MMP inhibition blockade (`D_P = 0.2775`), alongside linear velocity-vs-defect scaling (`r = 0.9495`) and empirical CV segmentation of bilateral eyes (`N = 2`, `|Delta s| = 0.0023`) and head width (`r = 0.9114`) on `xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg`, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_085_xenopus_craniofacial_remap.lean`. Overall 92.0/100 (faithfulness 91.9, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1009445 B, 2227×1863 px, artifact_sha256 a05e5ee5c81988c6442c768499a76a5f4e0a7ddae1b23bca3a0585f34a108cc2 (sha256 a05e5ee5c81988c6442c768499a76a5f4e0a7ddae1b23bca3a0585f34a108cc2), spec_fingerprint b508063893dc2ba283709bbd6f8bccfb0c0050e2d4a352a6be0037d6b7fbad04. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b508063893dc2ba283709bbd6f8bccfb0c0050e2d4a352a6be0037d6b7fbad04; artifact_sha256: a05e5ee5c81988c6442c768499a76a5f4e0a7ddae1b23bca3a0585f34a108cc2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/paper_citations.bib=f5f4d62c485aca75..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/scout_manifest.json=96534373d259eb28..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_reference.json=2656eaab51beb4ca..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg=8832f70a57f3d1c4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) Dev. Dyn. 241:863-878 craniofacial landmark tracking of eyes, nostrils/nares, and jaws across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45 to 65 showing goal-directed 'Picasso tadpole' normalization to froglet anatomy vs open-loop fixed-displacement vector failure | Proportional organ migration velocity scaling with displacement distance from target morphology (Vandenberg et al. 2012 Fig. 6) and restoration of bilateral facial symmetry | Pinet et al. (2019) Development 146:dev175893 thyroid-hormone-independent pre-metamorphic craniofacial remodeling and arrest under matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) inhibition (GM6001); reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE dx_i/dt = eta_MMP * [-K_i*(x_i - x_i^*) - sum_j C_ij*((x_i - x_j) - (x_i^* - x_j^*))] integrated via RK4 across NF stages 45->65 for 6 experimental regimes plus a 15x15 (alpha_pert, eta_MMP) morphospace grid | Automated PCA craniofacial axis, snout apex, 40-bin dorsal head width profile (r=0.9114), and bilateral dorsolateral eye detection (N=2 eyes, |Delta s|=0.0023) on xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal Procrustes craniofacial landmark coordinates (left/right eye, left/right naris, jaw midpoint) and reconstructed froglet head contour compared against dorsal Xenopus laevis specimen geometry; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element cartilage biomechanics of Meckel's/palatoquadrate chondrocytes or explicit collagen-I fibril cleavage kinetics." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple 3D cranial neural crest viscoelastic cartilage mechanics (Meckel's, ceratohyal, and palatoquadrate cartilages) to the 2D Procrustes landmark attractor.",
            "remediation needed: Incorporate explicit spatially resolved MMP-2/MMP-9 zymography fields along the optic nerve and jaw muscle insertions." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.92"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

